    <description>CODE-FLOW REVIEWED v30. FUN_00025CE8 calls descriptor 0x0AE62 through FUN_00015A42, then calls 0x0861A, multiplies the two byte factors, scales right by 7, and uses the result as a divisor/normalizer for FF837C before writing fields in the runtime object pointed by A2. Value-domain: load-normalization/controller factor vs speed; raw byte, not IAT correction as a proven physical name.. Proof: Ghidra disassembly only. Name is derived from caller, downstream RAM consumer and arithmetic/branch behavior; no Ronin/Wiki/KP/external XDF label is used as proof.</description>
